On Wed, 10 Nov 2004, Michael Lehotay wrote:

> Playing the unix version of NetHack I notice that everything black
> (orc armour, black dragons, etc) is blue. I know this used to be the
> case in older versions, but I thought it had been fixed. Am I wrong?
> Or is it just the version of NetHack I'm playing (on
> sonara.devnull.net)?

Nope, it seems like it is still that way. Or perhaps it is that way again.
They don't want a terminal with 8 colors to show bright black as dark
black. The code changes (if you were making your own binary for 16 colors)
would be minimal: switching the values of NO_COLOR and CLR_BLACK in
include/color.h, and making sure that win/tty/termcamp.c doesn't redefine
COLOR_BLACK as blue (it should be 0). At least that was my solution in
2000.

A better solution would be to have the videocolors option ported to the
unix version.

